# Images, Strings, Colors, Fonts

- Use **`AppAssets`** for all asset paths (`lib/core/constants/app_assets.dart`). Add new paths there only — do not introduce parallel image constant files.
- Use **`AppStrings`** for user-facing strings.
- Use **`AppColors`** for color values.
- Use **`AppFonts`** helpers for text styles.
- **One value, one constant:** Before adding a new member to **`AppStrings`**, **`AppAssets`**, or **`AppColors`**, search that file (and related typography helpers if applicable) for the **same literal** (same path, same hex/RGB, same copy). If it already exists, **reuse that existing name** — do **not** introduce another variable for an identical value.
- Add missing constants to the centralized classes before usage (only when no equivalent literal is already centralized).
- Do not hardcode asset paths, strings, colors, or inline text styles in UI code.
